{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.QHookDimensionBalanced","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.QHookDimensionBalanced","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.GeomSum","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Ring.Finset","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Factorial.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":15,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.QHookDimensionBalanced.dimQ_bal_eq_dimQ_of_twist_cancel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.QHookDimensionBalanced.dimQ_bal_eq_dimQ_of_twist_cancel","kind":"theorem","line":195,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/QHookDimensionBalanced.lean#L195-L209","doc":"**Balanced ↔ Gaussian hook-dimension cancellation (exact condition).** When\nthe accumulated hook-denominator twist matches the numerator (factorial) twist —\n`∏_{h ∈ hooks} q^{−(h−1)} = q^{−Σ_{i<n} i}` — the overall balanced twist cancels\nand `dim_bal(λ) = dim_{q^2}(λ)`. The hypothesis holds exactly when\n`Σ_{h ∈ hooks} (h−1) = Σ_{i<n} i` (for a genuine partition `λ ⊢ n`,\n`hooks.card = n`, this is `Σ h = n(n+1)/2` — true for hook / row / column shapes,\nfalse in general, e.g. `λ = (2,1)`; see the module docstring). Given\n`q ≠ 0`, `q^2 ≠ 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.QHookDimensionBalanced.hookprod_bal_split","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.QHookDimensionBalanced.hookprod_bal_split","kind":"theorem","line":184,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/QHookDimensionBalanced.lean#L184-L193","doc":"The hook-product twist split: `∏_{h} [h]_bal = (∏_{h} q^{−(h−1)}) · ∏_{h} [h]_{q^2}`.\nGiven `q ≠ 0`, `q^2 ≠ 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.QHookDimensionBalanced.dimQ_bal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.QHookDimensionBalanced.dimQ_bal","kind":"def","line":179,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/QHookDimensionBalanced.lean#L179-L182","doc":"The q-hook dimension in the balanced normalization:\n`dim_bal(λ) = [n]_bal! / ∏_{h ∈ hooks} [h]_bal`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.QHookDimensionBalanced.qFactPoly_bal_eq_twist","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.QHookDimensionBalanced.qFactPoly_bal_eq_twist","kind":"theorem","line":167,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/QHookDimensionBalanced.lean#L167-L177","doc":"**Factorial-level twist**: `[n]_bal! = q^{−Σ_{i<n} i} · qFactPoly(q^2) n`\n(written `(q⁻¹)^(Σ_{i<n} i) · …`). The per-factor monomial twists accumulate to\nthe triangular exponent `Σ_{i<n} i = n(n−1)/2`. Given `q ≠ 0`, `q^2 ≠ 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.QHookDimensionBalanced.qFactPoly_bal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.QHookDimensionBalanced.qFactPoly_bal","kind":"def","line":163,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/QHookDimensionBalanced.lean#L163-L165","doc":"The balanced q-factorial `[n]_bal! = ∏_{i<n} [i+1]_bal`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.QHookDimensionBalanced.qIntBal_eq_twist","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.QHookDimensionBalanced.qIntBal_eq_twist","kind":"theorem","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/QHookDimensionBalanced.lean#L133-L159","doc":"**The exact monomial twist relation** (turns the sibling docstring's prose\nclaim into a lemma): `[n]_bal = q^{−(n−1)} · qIntPoly(q^2) n`, written with\n`(q⁻¹)^(n−1)`. Given `q ≠ 0`, `q^2 ≠ 1`.\n\nVerified small cases: `n=1 ↦ 1 = 1`; `n=2 ↦ q + q⁻¹ = q⁻¹ · (1 + q^2)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.QHookDimensionBalanced.sub_inv_mul_qIntBal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.QHookDimensionBalanced.sub_inv_mul_qIntBal","kind":"theorem","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/QHookDimensionBalanced.lean#L124-L131","doc":"**Balanced defining identity**: `(q − q⁻¹) · [n]_bal = q^n − q^{−n}`. The\nclean multiplicative form of the balanced quantum integer (no `0/0`), given\n`q ≠ 0`, `q^2 ≠ 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.QHookDimensionBalanced.sub_inv_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.QHookDimensionBalanced.sub_inv_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/QHookDimensionBalanced.lean#L112-L122","doc":"`q − q⁻¹ ≠ 0` when `q ≠ 0` and `q^2 ≠ 1`. The only place the singularity of\nthe balanced form is excluded. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.QHookDimensionBalanced.qIntBal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.QHookDimensionBalanced.qIntBal","kind":"def","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/QHookDimensionBalanced.lean#L106-L110","doc":"The balanced quantum integer `[n]_bal = (q^n − q^{−n})/(q − q^{−1})`, over a\ngeneric `Field`. Singular only at `q^2 = 1` (where `q − q⁻¹ = 0`); the balanced\nidentities below carry `q ≠ 0`, `q^2 ≠ 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.QHookDimensionBalanced.dimQ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.QHookDimensionBalanced.dimQ","kind":"def","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/QHookDimensionBalanced.lean#L99-L102","doc":"The q-hook dimension `dim_q(λ) = [n]_q! / ∏_{h ∈ hooks} [h]_q` (polynomial\nnormalization). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.QHookDimensionBalanced.qFactPoly_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.QHookDimensionBalanced.qFactPoly_zero","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/QHookDimensionBalanced.lean#L96-L97","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.QHookDimensionBalanced.qFactPoly","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.QHookDimensionBalanced.qFactPoly","kind":"def","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/QHookDimensionBalanced.lean#L92-L94","doc":"The q-factorial `[n]_q! = ∏_{i<n} [i+1]_q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.QHookDimensionBalanced.sub_one_mul_qIntPoly","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.QHookDimensionBalanced.sub_one_mul_qIntPoly","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/QHookDimensionBalanced.lean#L84-L90","doc":"`(q − 1) · [n]_q = q^n − 1` — the geometric-sum relation in multiplicative\nform (over any commutative ring; no division). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.QHookDimensionBalanced.qIntPoly_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.QHookDimensionBalanced.qIntPoly_zero","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/QHookDimensionBalanced.lean#L81-L82","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.QHookDimensionBalanced.qIntPoly","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.QHookDimensionBalanced.qIntPoly","kind":"def","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/QHookDimensionBalanced.lean#L77-L79","doc":"The polynomial (Gaussian) q-integer `[n]_q = Σ_{i<n} q^i`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}